{:edb/db-before-t 1387 :edb/db-after-t 1388 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534700 50 #inst "2026-10-08T04:34:31.396Z" 13194139534700 true] [17592186100868 1020 #edb/ref 17592186304280 13194139534700 true] [17592186100868 1020 #edb/ref 17592186304287 13194139534700 true] [17592186100868 1020 #edb/ref 17592186304294 13194139534700 true] [17592186100876 1020 #edb/ref 17592186304273 13194139534700 true] [17592186100876 1020 #edb/ref 17592186304297 13194139534700 true] [17592186304273 1017 #edb/ref 17592186304274 13194139534700 true] [17592186304273 1089 "q-141092" 13194139534700 true] [17592186304273 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534700 true] [17592186304273 1100 "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-y\\operatorname{tan}⁡x.\n$$\n\n Which of the following is a solution to this equation?\n\n- $y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$\n- $y=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$\n- $y=-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$" 13194139534700 true] [17592186304273 1113 #uuid "6bc95deb-40f2-508a-aa44-de7fe1d1479e" 13194139534700 true] [17592186304273 1145 "For a function $f(x)$ to be a solution to a differential equation, it must satisfy the equation for all values of $x$ in the equation's domain.\n\nWe check each proposed solution by differentiating and substituting it into the original equation. \n\n- Differentiating $y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x,$ we get $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.$ Substituting into the original equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-y\\operatorname{tan}⁡x \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡x & \\overset{?}{=}-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\cdot \\operatorname{tan}⁡x \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡x & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis statement is *true*. Therefore, the function $y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ *is* a solution to our differential equation.\n\n- Differentiating $y=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x,$ we get $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.$ Substituting into the original equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-y\\operatorname{tan}⁡x \\\\ -3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x & \\overset{?}{=}-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\cdot \\operatorname{tan}⁡x \\\\ -3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x & =-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis statement is *true*. Therefore, the function $y=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ *is* a solution to our differential equation.\n\n- Differentiating $y=-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x,$ we get $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.$ Substituting into the original equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-y\\operatorname{tan}⁡x \\\\ 2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x & \\overset{?}{=}-(-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)\\cdot \\operatorname{tan}⁡x \\\\ 2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x & =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis statement is *true*. Therefore, the function $y=-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ *is* a solution to our differential equation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\"" 13194139534700 true] [17592186304274 1000 #edb/ref 17592186304275 13194139534700 true] [17592186304274 1000 #edb/ref 17592186304276 13194139534700 true] [17592186304274 1000 #edb/ref 17592186304277 13194139534700 true] [17592186304274 1000 #edb/ref 17592186304278 13194139534700 true] [17592186304274 1000 #edb/ref 17592186304279 13194139534700 true] [17592186304274 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534700 true] [17592186304274 1041 "selection" 13194139534700 true] [17592186304274 1104 #edb/ref 17592186304275 13194139534700 true] [17592186304274 1110 #uuid "d3231972-1caa-5cea-86d8-e37996473f0d" 13194139534700 true] [17592186304275 1034 "I, II, and III" 13194139534700 true] [17592186304275 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534700 true] [17592186304275 1111 #uuid "178e8522-f6d6-5615-a7db-e649a18d2cad" 13194139534700 true] [17592186304276 1034 "I only" 13194139534700 true] [17592186304276 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534700 true] [17592186304276 1111 #uuid "af616c88-26d1-5b72-b19c-57726ef