f 17592186304286 13194139534700 true] [17592186304281 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534700 true] [17592186304281 1041 "selection" 13194139534700 true] [17592186304281 1104 #edb/ref 17592186304285 13194139534700 true] [17592186304281 1110 #uuid "33a69b8c-cfd3-597e-be8d-e19a8a9f044c" 13194139534700 true] [17592186304282 1034 "2" 13194139534700 true] [17592186304282 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534700 true] [17592186304282 1111 #uuid "731f18bd-d7d6-51a1-b655-6def4699992a" 13194139534700 true] [17592186304283 1034 "1" 13194139534700 true] [17592186304283 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534700 true] [17592186304283 1111 #uuid "2f4284e2-6405-5af1-8e18-6ed7e5f0ceb2" 13194139534700 true] [17592186304284 1034 "-4" 13194139534700 true] [17592186304284 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534700 true] [17592186304284 1111 #uuid "c7868473-ef33-540e-afff-2111b32510ff" 13194139534700 true] [17592186304285 1034 "-1" 13194139534700 true] [17592186304285 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534700 true] [17592186304285 1111 #uuid "e80c9a44-9797-521d-8a6b-d9408f81ba46" 13194139534700 true] [17592186304286 1034 "-2" 13194139534700 true] [17592186304286 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534700 true] [17592186304286 1111 #uuid "00936aaf-aa47-5f4c-8b88-98068c612fa3" 13194139534700 true] [17592186304287 1017 #edb/ref 17592186304288 13194139534700 true] [17592186304287 1089 "q-141116" 13194139534700 true] [17592186304287 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534700 true] [17592186304287 1100 "Consider the following initial value problem\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-{y}^{2},\\,y(0)=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nYou're given that $y=\\frac{1}{A+x}$ is the solution to this initial value problem. What is the value of the constant $A?$" 13194139534700 true] [17592186304287 1113 #uuid "ea6ff592-81a4-59f3-84d6-c97bdc2e3a4f" 13194139534700 true] [17592186304287 1145 "We're given that $y=\\frac{1}{A+x}$ is the solution to the initial value problem. Therefore, it must satisfy the differential equation *and* the initial condition $y(0)=\\frac{1}{2}.$\n\nSubstituting the initial condition $y(0)=\\frac{1}{2}$ into our solution and solving for $A,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{1}{A+x} \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} & =\\frac{1}{A+0} \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} & =\\frac{1}{A} \\\\ A & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{1}{2+x}.\n$$" 13194139534700 true] [17592186304288 1000 #edb/ref 17592186304289 13194139534700 true] [17592186304288 1000 #edb/ref 17592186304290 13194139534700 true] [17592186304288 1000 #edb/ref 17592186304291 13194139534700 true] [17592186304288 1000 #edb/ref 17592186304292 13194139534700 true] [17592186304288 1000 #edb/ref 17592186304293 13194139534700 true] [17592186304288 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534700 true] [17592186304288 1041 "selection" 13194139534700 true] [17592186304288 1104 #edb/ref 17592186304291 13194139534700 true] [17592186304288 1110 #uuid "65cab405-7421-5b6f-a5c2-a8b4adeaf231" 13194139534700 true] [17592186304289 1034 "-\\frac{1}{2}" 13194139534700 true] [17592186304289 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534700 true] [17592186304289 1111 #uuid "7cf05be1-4507-5c1a-8a3c-31ab08cc9d20" 13194139534700 true] [17592186304290 1034 "\\frac{1}{2}" 13194139534700 true] [17592186304290 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534700 true] [17592186304290 1111 #uuid "3c94db7b-8874-5d6d-b048-2fd3ff11f860" 13194139534700 true] [17592186304291 1034 "2" 13194139534700 true] [17592186304291 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534700 true] [17592186304291 1111 #uuid "191114dc-6acc-568b-9cc5-d71bfeca996b" 13194139534700 true] [17592186304292 1034 "1" 13194139534700 true] [17592186304292 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534700 true] [17592186304292 1111 #uuid "6632709a-3d7c-5ba7-a42f-db9b5d4aec6d" 13194139534700 true] [17592186304293 1034 "-1" 13194139534700 true] [17592186304293 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534700 true] [17592186304293 1111 #uuid "a005a8c3-1eb7-5608-bf28-850aabbb8a35" 13194139534700 true] [17592186304294 1017 #edb/ref 17592186304295 13194139534700 true] [17592186304294 1089 "q-352660" 13194139534700 true] [17592186304294 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534700 true] [17592186304294 1100 "Consider the following initial value problem\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-\\frac{4y}{x},\\,y(2)=\\frac{3}{4}.\n$$\n\nYou're given that $y=\\frac{A}{{x}^{4}}$ is the solution to this initial value problem. What is the value of the constant $A?$\n\n$A=${{field-1}}" 13194139534700 true] [17592186304294 1113 #uuid "0ad1b80f-f6b4-5a82-9600-dba1f5e03f4d" 13194139534700 true] [17592186304294 1145 "We're given that $y=\\frac{A}{{x}^{4}}$ is the solution to the initial value problem. Therefore, it must satisfy the differential equation *and* the initial condition $y(2)=\\frac{3}{4}.$\n\nSubstituting the initial condition $y(2)=\\frac{3}{4}$ into our solution and solving for $A,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{A}{{x}^{4}} \\\\ \\frac{3}{4} & =\\frac{A}{{2}^{4}} \\\\ \\frac{3}{4} & =\\frac{A}{16} \\\\ A & =12.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534700 true] [17592186304295 1000 #edb/ref 17592186304296 13194139534700 true] [17592186304295 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534700 true] [17592186304295 1041 "field-1" 13194139534700 true] [17592186304295 1104 #edb/ref 17592186304296 13194139534700 true] [17592186304295 1110 #uuid "c7462996-4474-52b4-8b55-d9744d03b6e6" 13194139534700 true] [17592186304296 1034 "12" 13194139534700 true] [17592186304296 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534700 true] [17592186304296 1111 #uuid "283c827a-e42f-5a0a-a767-1f40d3564e0c" 13194139534700 true] [17592186304297 1017 #edb/ref 17592186304298 13194139534700 true] [17592186304297 1089 "q-79330" 13194139534700 true] [17592186304297 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534700 true] [17592186304297 1100 "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=4y.\n$$\n\n Which of the following is a solution to this equation?\n\n- $y={e}^{-4x}$\n- $y={e}^{4x}$\n- $y=4{e}^{x}$" 13194139534700 true] [17592186304297 1113 #uuid "df42d33c-ab0b-52f4-82a5-1108ad30f682" 13194139534700 true] [17592186304297 1145 "For a function $f(x)$ to be a solution to a differential equation, it must satisfy the equation for all values of $x$ in the equation's domain.\n\nWe check each proposed solution by differentiating and substituting it into the original equation. \n\n- Differentiating $y={e}^{-4x},$ we get $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-4{e}^{-4x}.$ Substituting into the original equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =4y \\\\ -4{e}^{-4x} & \\overset{?}{=}4{e}^{-4x} \\\\ 0 & \\ne 8{e}^{-4x}.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis statement is *not true* for all $x.$ Therefore, the function $y={e}^{-4x}$ is *not* a solution to our differential equation.\n\n- Differentiating $y={e}^{4x},$ we get $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=4{e}^{4x}.$ Substituting into the original equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =4y \\\\ 4{e}^{4x} & =4{e}^{4x}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis statement is *true*. Therefore, the function $y={e}^{4x}$ *is* a solution to our differential equation.\n\n- Differentiating $y=4{e}^{x},$ we get $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=4{e}^{x}.$ Substituting into the original equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =4y \\\\ 4{e}^{x} & \\overset{?}{=}4(4{e}^{x}) \\\\ 4{e}^{x} & \\overset{?}{=}16{e}^{x} \\\\ 0 & \\ne 12{e}^{x}.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis statement is *not true* for all $x.$ Therefore, the function $y=4{e}^{x}$ is *not* a solution to our differential equation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" 13194139534700 true] [17592186304298 1000 #edb/ref 17592186304299 13194139534700 true] [17592186304298 1000 #edb/ref 17592186304300 13194139534700 true] [17592186304298 1000 #edb/ref 17592186304301 13194139534700 true] [17592186304298 1000 #edb/ref 17592